[
        #[
                version: 1.0.0
                date: to :date "2026-10-31T12:39:37+00:00"
                link: "https://github.com/drkameleon/mimetypes.art/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
                details: #[
                        size: 119346
                        files: 10
                        readme: {
                                <h1 align="center">
                                    Mimetypes
                                </h1>
                                
                                <p align="center">
                                     <i>MIME content type registry & recognition package for Arturo</i> 
                                     <br><br>
                                     <img src="https://img.shields.io/github/license/drkameleon/mimetypes.art?style=for-the-badge">
                                    <a href="https://github.com/arturo-lang/arturo" style="text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;"><img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/language-Arturo-6A156B.svg?style=for-the-badge" alt="Language"/></a>
                                    <a href="https://github.com/drkameleon/mimetypes.art/actions/workflows/ci.yml" style="text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;"><img src="https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/drkameleon/mimetypes.art/ci.yml?branch=main&style=for-the-badge" alt="Build Status"/></a>
                                </p>
                                
                                --- 
                                 
                                <!--ts-->
                                
                                * [What does this package do?](#what-does-this-package-do)
                                * [How do I use it?](#how-do-i-use-it)
                                * [Function Reference](#function-reference)
                                * [Updating the database](#updating-the-database)
                                * [License](#license)   
                                
                                <!--te-->
                                 
                                ---
                                
                                ### What does this package do?
                                
                                This package provides an ample (2000+) entry database of MIME content types and their corresponding extensions and allows to easily look up the suitable MIME types by file extension (or file path). It also supports the reverse operation: look up possible extensions, based on a given MIME type.
                                
                                > [!TIP]
                                > For the data, the package has been based on the very useful list compiled by the [mime-db](https://github.com/jshttp/mime-db) project.
                                
                                ### How do I use it?
                                
                                Simply `import` it and use the included `mimetype` function:
                                
                                ```arturo
                                import "mimetypes"!
                                
                                mimetype "jpg"              ; => ["image/jpeg"]
                                mimetype "somefile.jpg"     ; => ["image/jpeg"]
                                mimetype "boom"             ; => []
                                
                                mimetype.best "photo.JPG"   ; => "image/jpeg"
                                mimetype.best "file.xml"    ; => "application/xml"
                                mimetype.best "boom"        ; => null
                                
                                mimetype.extensions "image/jpeg"
                                ; => ["jpg","jpeg","jpe"]
                                
                                mimetype.extensions.best "audio/mpeg"
                                ; => "mp3"
                                ```
                                
                                > [!IMPORTANT]
                                > In case no suitable MIME type has been found for a given extension/path, or if the given MIME type isn't associated with any known extensions, then `mimetype` will return an empty block - or `null`, if `.best` is used!
                                
                                > [!NOTE]
                                > Results are always ordered by preference (most suitable first) - and that's what `.best` picks:
                                > - for MIME types (by extension), using the same scoring as the [mime-types](https://github.com/jshttp/mime-types) package
                                > - for extensions (by MIME type), using mime-db's own order - except for `audio/aac` → `aac`, `audio/mpeg` → `mp3` and `video/quicktime` → `mov`
                                
                                ### Function reference
                                
                                #### `mimetype`
                                
                                ##### Description
                                
                                get mimetype(s) from given extension/filepath
                                
                                ##### Usage
                                
                                <pre>
                                <b>mimetype</b> <ins>location</ins> <i>:string</i>
                                </pre>
                                
                                ##### Attributes
                                
                                | Option | Type(s) | Description |
                                |----|----|----|
                                | extensions |  | get possible file extensions for given mimetype instead | 
                                | best |  | get only the best match (or null, if none) |
                                
                                ##### Returns
                                
                                - *:block*
                                - *:string* (when `.best` is used and a match has been found)
                                - *:null* (when `.best` is used and no match has been found)
                                
                                <hr/>
                                
                                ### Updating the database
                                
                                Both `src/mimedb.art` and `src/extdb.art` are generated from [mime-db](https://github.com/jshttp/mime-db) - to update them, bump `mimedbVersion` in `tools/generate.art` and run:
                                
                                ```bash
                                arturo tools/generate.art
                                ```
                                
